This patch is needed because Solaris C++ headers and compiler behavior expose a
char versus int8_t specialization clash in the generated Temporal C API helper
header.

What it does:
- skips the conflicting String converter specialization on Solaris

Why it is needed:
- without it, the C++ binding header fails to compile due to duplicate
  specialization logic

--- a/v8-147.4.0/third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/vendor/temporal_capi-v0_2/bindings/cpp/temporal_rs/diplomat_runtime.hpp
+++ b/v8-147.4.0/third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/vendor/temporal_capi-v0_2/bindings/cpp/temporal_rs/diplomat_runtime.hpp
@@ -392,1 +392,3 @@
+#if !defined(__sun)
 MAKE_SLICE_CONVERTERS(String, char)
+#endif
